WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:05.689
We haven't talked about any press briefings
by Joe Biden's White House press secretary,

00:00:05.689 --> 00:00:07.519
Jen Psaki, for a bit.

00:00:07.519 --> 00:00:11.440
We've been tied up with other things like
covid stimulus and much more.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:16.029
But I want to look at one today because it's
quite interesting what's going on.

00:00:16.029 --> 00:00:24.220
First of all, this first clip is CBS reporter
Lijiang asking Jen Psaki to respond to claims

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:28.690
that Joe Biden has opened the border wide
open and people are just pouring, pouring

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:29.690
in.

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:31.810
And it wasn't happening under Donald Trump,
but it is now.

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:35.710
Now, it's really important to remember that
even though Donald Trump didn't build the

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:42.070
wall during his presidency, he would regularly
claim that he built it and that the imaginary

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:45.559
wall was responsible for record low undocumented
crossings.

00:00:45.559 --> 00:00:50.920
Now, bear with me because this requires assuming
multiple lies are true to understand their

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:52.550
position.

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:56.200
If you believe Trump, that he built the wall.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:01:01.620
And of course, if you believe that Joe Biden
hasn't taken down that wall, you would have

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:06.560
to imagine that the job that the wall was
doing at keeping people out when Trump was

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:10.020
president is still keeping people out today.

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:16.650
But the narrative has shifted into Biden has
opened the border and people with diseases

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:17.650
are pouring in.

00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:20.930
The Nazi rhetoric that we talked about earlier.

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:26.700
And here Jen Psaki smartly goes after the
idea of Americans are saying and gets reporter

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:32.130
Wijk Zhang to admit, well, I mean, Trump Trump
is the one saying it.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:34.560
And Jen Psaki quickly dispenses with the nonsense.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:41.480
But a lot of Americans are saying that the
surges are happening under President Biden's

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:44.810
watch after he reversed some previous policies.

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:50.280
So does the administration take any accountability
for what's happening for the Americans?

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:56.440
Well, I know you don't answer to him, but
the former president just released a statement

00:01:56.440 --> 00:02:01.360
saying that the Biden administration must
act immediately to end the border nightmare

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:04.649
that they have unleashed on Chinese President
Trump.

00:02:04.649 --> 00:02:10.249
Yes, we don't take our advice or counsel from
former President Trump on immigration policy,

00:02:10.249 --> 00:02:15.260
which was not only inhumane but ineffective
over the last four years.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:17.079
We're going to chart our own path forward.

00:02:17.079 --> 00:02:21.620
And that includes treating children with humanity
and respect and ensuring they're safe when

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:22.920
they cross our borders.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:23.920
This is just so funny.

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:26.870
And I'm not even really looking to criticize
Zhang.

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:30.269
I think that she's asking what are meant to
be tough questions.

00:02:30.269 --> 00:02:32.409
She asked them of Kayleigh McEnany.

00:02:32.409 --> 00:02:34.090
She asks them of Jen Psaki.

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:38.879
It's more a lesson in how vapid and politically
biased these claims are.

00:02:38.879 --> 00:02:45.519
Where from Trump's last day to Biden's tenth
day, Republicans started wildly claiming Joe

00:02:45.519 --> 00:02:47.510
Biden has opened the border wide open.

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:51.139
Joe Biden has dramatically changed what's
going on at the border when, in fact, if there

00:02:51.139 --> 00:02:55.870
is a real critique of Joe Biden here, it's
that he hasn't changed that much about what's

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:59.769
going on at the border since taking over,
despite promises to do so.

00:02:59.769 --> 00:03:01.249
We talked about that early last week.

00:03:01.249 --> 00:03:04.419
I won't rehash the entire conversation.

00:03:04.419 --> 00:03:08.639
Just a few more funny examples of high jinks
at the latest press briefing.

00:03:08.639 --> 00:03:14.489
Here's a reporter asking why Joe Biden hasn't
done a solo press briefing yet.

00:03:14.489 --> 00:03:21.459
So we're 45 days into the Biden presidency,
and he has yet to hold a pressure at this

00:03:21.459 --> 00:03:23.349
point in past presidencies.

00:03:23.349 --> 00:03:29.019
Every president, you know, proudly Reagan
had addressed reporters several dozen, multiple

00:03:29.019 --> 00:03:30.019
times.

00:03:30.019 --> 00:03:33.379
So why the delay and why do we expect the
president to hold a press conference?

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:37.449
Well, first, as all of you know, the president
takes questions several times a week.

00:03:37.449 --> 00:03:41.739
He took questions actually twice yesterday,
which is an opportunity for the people covering

00:03:41.739 --> 00:03:45.379
the White House to ask him about whatever
news is happening on any given day.

00:03:45.379 --> 00:03:50.060
We look forward to holding a full press conference
in the coming weeks before the end of the

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:51.060
month.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:52.569
And we're working on setting a final date
for that.

00:03:52.569 --> 00:03:54.430
And as soon as we do, we will let you all
know.

00:03:54.430 --> 00:03:57.319
I can really kind of see both sides on this.

00:03:57.319 --> 00:04:00.949
I mean, certainly presidents should be taking
questions from the press.

00:04:00.949 --> 00:04:07.159
It is true that while you usually see both
the president and their press secretary taking

00:04:07.159 --> 00:04:11.049
questions in the press briefing room, Biden
hasn't done that yet.

00:04:11.049 --> 00:04:15.449
But Biden is holding covid related and other
events almost daily.

00:04:15.449 --> 00:04:18.799
And he doesn't take questions at all of them,
but he's taking questions a whole bunch of

00:04:18.799 --> 00:04:22.979
times in his first six weeks in office sometimes,
as Jen Psaki points out, more than once in

00:04:22.979 --> 00:04:23.979
a day.

00:04:23.979 --> 00:04:27.759
OK, I mean, the point is that the press in
the midst of what is at least for now, a very

00:04:27.759 --> 00:04:32.860
popular presidency, all things considered,
Biden again, highest initial approval of any

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:38.110
president in 30 years, almost 70 percent covid
relief, support, et cetera.

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:43.199
The press are having to sort of manufacture
problems or scandals, and it's not going super

00:04:43.199 --> 00:04:44.199
well, I.

00:04:44.199 --> 00:04:47.669
That there are plenty of fair critiques they
could go after, but they're going after other

00:04:47.669 --> 00:04:48.669
things.

00:04:48.669 --> 00:04:54.139
One other example, Fox News reporter stepping
away briefly from the Dr Seuss scandal, which

00:04:54.139 --> 00:04:59.379
has been 24/7 on Fox News for about a week
now to push this crisis at the border thing.

00:04:59.379 --> 00:05:04.400
And I think what Jen Psaki does well here,
she doesn't do everything well, but this she

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:05.569
did well.

00:05:05.569 --> 00:05:10.970
She refuses to escalate into the hysterical
language that the reporter from FOX is baiting

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:11.970
her with.

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:12.970
Take a look.

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:17.560
Are there any discussions within the White
House about reversing the policy of allowing

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:20.469
all unaccompanied children into the United
States?

00:05:20.469 --> 00:05:22.469
No, not at all.

00:05:22.469 --> 00:05:30.050
So I guess, is the plan then to take in and
safely and humanely find a home for an unlimited

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:32.370
number of unaccompanied children?

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:37.900
I think this issue requires us taking a step
back as human beings and as mothers, of which

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:38.900
I am one.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:42.090
I know there are many in the room or many
at home.

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:43.090
These kids are coming.

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:44.909
They are fleeing prosecution.

00:05:44.909 --> 00:05:49.800
They are fleeing difficult circumstances in
their home country when they come here.

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:54.469
All where we're talking about here is ensuring
that they are treated safely, they are not

00:05:54.469 --> 00:05:59.039
trafficked, they are not sent back on a unsafe
journey.

00:05:59.039 --> 00:06:00.039
That's what we're talking about.

00:06:00.039 --> 00:06:03.539
When they come when these kids come in, it
doesn't mean they are ensured that they get

00:06:03.539 --> 00:06:04.539
to stay.

00:06:04.539 --> 00:06:07.159
They go through the processing system that
everyone goes through.

00:06:07.159 --> 00:06:12.350
But we want to ensure that that is done by
treating them humanely and with respect.

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:14.410
Many of them will be sent back home eventually.

00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:18.129
But we're talking about how we treat them
as they come in the country.

00:06:18.129 --> 00:06:22.539
Now, I have been critical of Joe Biden on
immigration.

00:06:22.539 --> 00:06:27.479
I think his one executive order on stopping
removals, which was stopped by a judge, wasn't

00:06:27.479 --> 00:06:28.479
enough.

00:06:28.479 --> 00:06:31.409
He should have done another one using a different
legal rationale.

00:06:31.409 --> 00:06:33.650
I talked about that last Monday.

00:06:33.650 --> 00:06:38.039
But the hysterical critique, that policy has
dramatically changed in six weeks, resulting

00:06:38.039 --> 00:06:40.830
in people just now pouring in uncontrollably.

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:45.189
It's silly the projection that the Fox News
reporter cites about one hundred and ten thousand

00:06:45.189 --> 00:06:47.409
or whatever that number was.

00:06:47.409 --> 00:06:49.349
We had similar projections under Trump.

00:06:49.349 --> 00:06:54.259
The point is under Trump, what they're counting
on is that under Trump, nobody who watches

00:06:54.259 --> 00:06:59.840
Fox knew that these are just the normal numbers
that immigration authorities are dealing with.

00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:05.840
So when the Fox News reporter there says the
expectation is 110000 kids will come, it sounds

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:09.270
shocking, but there's nothing particularly
notable about those numbers.

00:07:09.270 --> 00:07:13.470
This is a huge country and those are the same
numbers we were seeing under Donald Trump.

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:21.379
So we'll see if and how the tone and tenor
of the briefings change over time from now.

00:07:21.379 --> 00:07:22.520
This is what it's been like.

00:07:22.520 --> 00:08:18.999
And Jen Psaki handling it relatively well,
The David Pakman 

00:08:18.999 --> 00:08:32.580
Show at David Pakman dot com.

